***acceptance tests***

# extra-key
The file `extra_frontmatter_key.plain` with the keys `module`, `func_id` and `description` raises exactly `Plain syntax error: Test plain file 'extra_frontmatter_key.plain' has the frontmatter key `description:`; only `module:` and `func_id:` are allowed.`.

# missing-func-id
The file `missing_func_id.plain` with only `module: task-manager` raises exactly `Plain syntax error: Test plain file 'missing_func_id.plain' has no `func_id:` key in its frontmatter.`.

# module-not-a-string
The file `module_not_a_string.plain` with `module: [a, b]` raises exactly `Plain syntax error: Test plain file 'module_not_a_string.plain': the frontmatter key `module:` must be a non-empty string.`.

# invalid-yaml
The text `---`, `module: [`, `---` named `broken.plain` raises `PlainSyntaxError` holding `Test plain file 'broken.plain' has invalid frontmatter`.
